From: herminio.hernandezjr@gmail.com
Date: Wed=2C 15 Jun 2016 22:02:29 -0700
Subject: Re: [Stretch] Status for architecture qualification
To: hector.oron@gmail.com
CC: niels@thykier.net=3B debian-admin@lists.debian.org=3B team@security.deb=
ian.org=3B debian-release@lists.debian.org=3B debian-ports@lists.debian.org=
=3B debian-wb-team@lists.debian.org=3B riku@debian.org

I know there are still powerpc users who run Debian. I am one of them and l=
ove to see it continue. How can I help?
Thanks!
On Wed=2C Jun 15=2C 2016 at 5:12 PM=2C Hector Oron <hector.oron@gmail.com> =
wrote:
[Add to CC debian-wb-team@ and riku@debian.org]
=0A=

=0A=
Hello=2C
=0A=

=0A=
2016-06-05 12:01 GMT+02:00 Niels Thykier <niels@thykier.net>:
=0A=
> Hi members of DSA=2C Security=2C RT and all porters.
=0A=
>
=0A=
> While the freeze still seem far away=2C I think it is time to start with
=0A=
> the architecture qualifications.
=0A=

=0A=
Excellent! Thanks
=0A=

=0A=
I tried to follow the follow-up thread=2C ended up watching an hour
=0A=
video which was quite fun and forgot all details. :-)
=0A=

=0A=
I have put up the classical wiki page for Stretch at:
=0A=
  https://wiki.debian.org/ArchiveQualification/Stretch
=0A=

=0A=
Please review and comment if required.
=0A=

=0A=
> For starters=2C here are the architectures we are aware of:
=0A=
>
=0A=
>  * amd64=2C i386=2C armel=2C armhf=2C arm64=2C mips=2C mipsel=2C powerpc=
=2C ppc64el=2C
=0A=
>    s390x
=0A=
>    - *No* blockers at this time from RT=2C DSA nor security.
=0A=
>    - s390=2C ppc64el and all arm ports have DSA concerns.
=0A=

=0A=
I understand s390x and ppc64el DSA concerns have been clarified
=0A=
in-list and those concerns are due to nature of the architecture.
=0A=

=0A=
For the ARM ports=2C which have also been clarified=2C let me re-confirm:
=0A=
 * arm64 port has remote power and remote console available=2C plus
=0A=
geo-redundancy=2C hardware is available and there is more hardware
=0A=
coming in the pipeline. I am unsure why it is listed with multiple DSA
=0A=
concerns=2C that surprises me (with DSA and ARM porter hats). The port
=0A=
currently has 4 machines up=2C one down waiting to be replaced=2C in total
=0A=
5 and more coming.
=0A=
 * armhf/armel ports share hardware=2C we currently have 6 machines up
=0A=
with remote power and remote console (of course that being development
=0A=
boards is not so nice as server remote management goodies). Some
=0A=
machines require a button press but local admins are great and always
=0A=
happy to help.
=0A=

=0A=
If none steps up explaining what are DSA concerns on the ARM
=0A=
architectures=2C please update status requalification page dropping
=0A=
those concerns. [DSA hat on]
=0A=

=0A=
I see armel has one porter listed=2C if more are needed=2C please add
=0A=
myself and Riku Voipio (armel buildd maints). [ARM hat on]
=0A=
I see arm64/armhf are covered porterwise however there should be more
=0A=
porters available if needed.
=0A=

=0A=
>    - armel has a RT concern about lack of buildds (only 2)
=0A=

=0A=
>From the above comment: "armhf/armel ports share hardware=2C we
=0A=
currently have 6 machines up"
=0A=

=0A=
>  * mips64el (NEW)
=0A=
>    - No DSA buildd (RT blocker)
=0A=

=0A=
As far as I can see mips64el is using shared builds with mipsel port
=0A=
hardware=2C those machines are DSA.
=0A=

=0A=
>    - Rebuild after import not complete (RT Blocker)
=0A=

=0A=
Is there a list of packages that should be rebuilt?
=0A=

=0A=
>    - Not yet in testing (due to the above).
=0A=

=0A=
Please let's work on getting it in testing ASAP I think the above
=0A=
blockers can be worked out quite reasonably.
=0A=

=0A=
>  * kfreebsd-i386=2C kfreebsd-amd64
=0A=
>    - Not included in Jessie due to lack of sustainable man-power (RT
=0A=
>      blocker)
=0A=
>    - No news of the situation having changed
=0A=
>    - If there is no news on the situation after DebConf16=2C I will
=0A=
>      assume kfreebsd-* will not target Stretch.
=0A=

=0A=
Who has been keeping it up for stretch? (As a side note Stephen
=0A=
Chamberlain=2C Christoph Egger and many other people keep working on it)
=0A=
Not sure if those arches have more or less manpower than powerpc (in
=0A=
example). I think it would be great to make a call here=2C we either
=0A=
move kfreebsd ports to debian-ports infrastructure or go for the
=0A=
release with it.
=0A=

=0A=
While working out ArchitectureQualification/Stretch wiki page I
=0A=
believe everything is mostly fine for release=2C however I got a
=0A=
personal concern on powerpc architecture. Is it well maintained? Does
=0A=
it have porters? Does it have users? Does it still make sense to carry
=0A=
along?
=0A=

=0A=
Another concern (DSA) which I have added and explained in the wiki
=0A=
page is the lack of georedundancy for the 'mips' port. Verbatim copy
=0A=
from wiki follows:
=0A=
"mips: It has 5 buildds in the same datacenter=2C current hardware are
=0A=
routers or development boards which makes it very difficult to ship to
=0A=
other places. The host providing redundancy (lucatelli) at UBC-ECE
=0A=
must be decomissioned ASAP=2C leaving the port in a situation of not
=0A=
geographic redundancy. However advanced plans exists to deploy mips
=0A=
hardware in other data centers RSN."
=0A=

=0A=
I'll keep you posted whenever there is progress on that area. I do not
=0A=
believe it should be a blocker for release=2C but we must ensure geo
=0A=
redundancy first.
=0A=

=0A=
> Beyond mips64el=2C we are not aware of any new architectures for Stretch.
=0A=

=0A=
Could you please check with sparc64 porters? I think some of them
=0A=
commented on the follow ups.
=0A=

=0A=
Regards=2C
=0A=
--
=0A=
 H=E9ctor Or=F3n  -.. . -... .. .- -.   -.. . ...- . .-.. --- .--. . .-.
=0A=

=0A=

